fftw3-hpx (2026-10-23)
=====================

The hpx/ directory ports FFTW 3.3.11's distributed-memory library to HPX
localities, collectives and channels. The default path retains the original
algorithms and planner hooks. FFTW's existing thread callback runs worker jobs on HPX
large-stack threads. Configure with --enable-hpx --enable-threads and the HPX
pkg-config path; double, single and long-double precision are supported.
See hpx/README.md for the SPMD application contract and build/test commands,
and hpx/VALIDATION.md for source provenance, exact checks and local results.
The bridge now receives large pairwise messages directly into FFTW-owned
storage after exchanging readiness notifications. FFTW retains ownership of
its allocations. Profiling identified the removed final receive copy as about
70 percent of the previously measured HPX/MPI timing gap. A lean HPX build
also removes optional instrumentation while retaining the MPI parcelport.
The 10 ms tuning cohort measured HPX at 3.489 seconds versus MPI
controls of 3.279 and 3.312 seconds, with a 10 ms HPX idle-backoff cap. The
remaining overhead in that cohort was 5.4-6.4 percent; the report records run variation and
the increased runtime CPU activity observed with the shorter cap.
A later comparison measured 3.489 seconds with the same cap and 3.487 seconds
with backoff disabled, versus MPI controls of 3.325 and 3.360 seconds.
Disabling backoff did not materially improve HPX time; its 3.8-4.9 percent
gap to those MPI controls remains unresolved. A slower repeated HPX control
limits conclusions from this fixed-order run. The documented cap stays 10 ms.
The subsequent all-to-all transpose experiment measured 12.786 and 12.805
seconds, versus 3.498 and 3.499 seconds for HPX pairwise and 3.353 and 3.371
seconds for FFTW-MPI. HPX all_to_all was 3.65-3.66 times slower than pairwise
and 3.79-3.82 times slower than MPI. Pairwise remains the default; the optional
collective exchange and its exact evidence are documented in
benchmarks/queenbee/remaining_overhead/all_to_all/README.md.
See benchmarks/queenbee/remaining_overhead/README.md for the unchanged
1024-cubed QueenBee comparison, all timing cohorts, remaining overhead,
correctness checks and exact build/runtime settings. Earlier pooled-receive
and original results remain in benchmarks/queenbee/optimization/README.md and
benchmarks/queenbee/README.md. hpx/MPI_MAPPING.md lists the MPI calls replaced
and the scope of their HPX replacements.

This repository starts from the official release tarball, including its
already-generated codelets:
  https://fftw.org/fftw-3.3.11.tar.gz
SHA256:
  5630c24cdeb33b131612f7eb4b1a9934234754f9f388ff8617458d0be6f239a1
Do not use the upstream Git bootstrap instructions below for this port;
its release sources build with autotools without OCaml or maintainer mode.

TCP is permitted only between localities on the same server. Cross-server
runs must use HPX's MPI parcelport with TCP disabled. The supplied local
check targets launch processes on one server only.

